.TH HOSTNAME 1N UniSoft
.SH NAME
hostname \- set or print name of current host system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hostname
[ nameofhost ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I hostname\^
command prints the name of the current host, as given before the
"login" prompt.
The super-user can set the hostname by giving an argument; this
is usually done in the startup script 
.B /etc/rc.
.SH SEE ALSO
gethostname(2N), sethostname(2N)
.\"N	 @(#)hostname.1N	 5.2 of 7/12/84
